    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Question\n\nHello,\r\nThank for all your hardwork on this amazing plugin. I want to exclude certain items which contains certain pattern in their names and reading the docs I did the following, however this doesn't seem to work.\r\n\r\n```\r\n{\r\n    \"echasnovski/mini.files\",\r\n    opts = function(_, opts)\r\n      return vim.tbl_deep_extend(\"force\", opts, {\r\n        content = {\r\n          filter = function(fs_entry)\r\n            print(string.find(fs_entry.name, \"dist-info\"))\r\n            if string.find(fs_entry.name, \"dist-info\") then\r\n              return false\r\n            end\r\n            return true\r\n          end,\r\n        },\r\n    end,\r\n  }\r\n```\r\n\r\nHow can I fix this ?",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.files</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Hello,<br>\nThank for all your hardwork on this amazing plugin. I want to exclude certain items which contains certain pattern in their names and reading the docs I did the following, however this doesn't seem to work.</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"{\n    &quot;echasnovski/mini.files&quot;,\n    opts = function(_, opts)\n      return vim.tbl_deep_extend(&quot;force&quot;, opts, {\n        content = {\n          filter = function(fs_entry)\n            print(string.find(fs_entry.name, &quot;dist-info&quot;))\n            if string.find(fs_entry.name, &quot;dist-info&quot;) then\n              return false\n            end\n            return true\n          end,\n        },\n    end,\n  }\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">{\n    \"echasnovski/mini.files\",\n    opts = function(_, opts)\n      return vim.tbl_deep_extend(\"force\", opts, {\n        content = {\n          filter = function(fs_entry)\n            print(string.find(fs_entry.name, \"dist-info\"))\n            if string.find(fs_entry.name, \"dist-info\") then\n              return false\n            end\n            return true\n          end,\n        },\n    end,\n  }\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">How can I fix this ?</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.files\nQuestion\nHello,\nThank for all your hardwork on this amazing plugin. I want to exclude certain items which contains certain pattern in their names and reading the docs I did the following, however this doesn't seem to work.\n{\n    \"echasnovski/mini.files\",\n    opts = function(_, opts)\n      return vim.tbl_deep_extend(\"force\", opts, {\n        content = {\n          filter = function(fs_entry)\n            print(string.find(fs_entry.name, \"dist-info\"))\n            if string.find(fs_entry.name, \"dist-info\") then\n              return false\n            end\n            return true\n          end,\n        },\n    end,\n  }\n\nHow can I fix this ?",
