            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "It should filter as expected. The issue here is `\"dist-info\"` pattern does not find `dist-info` string verbatim because `-` is a special Lua pattern quantifier (`:h lua-patternitem`). The following `filter` entry should do what you expect it to:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nfilter = function(fs_entry) return fs_entry.name:find('dist%-info') == nil end\r\n```",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">It should filter as expected. The issue here is <code class=\"notranslate\">\"dist-info\"</code> pattern does not find <code class=\"notranslate\">dist-info</code> string verbatim because <code class=\"notranslate\">-</code> is a special Lua pattern quantifier (<code class=\"notranslate\">:h lua-patternitem</code>). The following <code class=\"notranslate\">filter</code> entry should do what you expect it to:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"filter = function(fs_entry) return fs_entry.name:find('dist%-info') == nil end\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-en\">filter</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">fs_entry</span>) <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">fs_entry</span>.<span class=\"pl-en\">name</span>:<span class=\"pl-c1\">find</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>dist%-info<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>) <span class=\"pl-k\">==</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">nil</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span></pre></div>",
            "bodyText": "It should filter as expected. The issue here is \"dist-info\" pattern does not find dist-info string verbatim because - is a special Lua pattern quantifier (:h lua-patternitem). The following filter entry should do what you expect it to:\nfilter = function(fs_entry) return fs_entry.name:find('dist%-info') == nil end",
